  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Pattern: Xを{率|ひき}いる.\n\nUSAGE:\nA formal verb used to describe leading a group of people in an organized capacity. Common with military, sports, business, and organizational contexts. Not used for casual or everyday \"leading\" like showing someone the way.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- チームを{率|ひき}いる: to lead a team\n- {軍|ぐん}を{率|ひき}いる: to command an army\n- {部下|ぶか}を{率|ひき}いる: to lead subordinates\n- {代表団|だいひょうだん}を{率|ひき}いる: to head a delegation\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{導|みちび}く focuses on guiding or showing the way. {率|ひき}いる emphasizes being at the head of a group and directing them as a leader.",
